# Security Standards

Apply the following security patterns from the system-design-prompt-kit:

## OWASP Top 10 Awareness
- A01: Broken Access Control — enforce authorization on every endpoint
- A02: Cryptographic Failures — use strong algorithms, never roll your own crypto
- A03: Injection — parameterize all queries, sanitize all output
- A07: Authentication Failures — use proven libraries, enforce MFA where possible

## Input Validation
- Validate type, length, range, and format on all user inputs
- Use allowlists over denylists
- Validate on the server side even if client-side validation exists
- Sanitize output to prevent XSS (context-aware encoding)

## Authentication
- Use OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect for token-based auth
- Store passwords with bcrypt/scrypt/argon2 (never MD5/SHA1)
- Implement token refresh with short-lived access tokens (15 min)
- Use secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookies for session tokens

## Secrets Management
- Never commit secrets to version control
- Use environment variables or a vault (HashiCorp Vault, Azure Key Vault, AWS Secrets Manager)
- Rotate secrets on a schedule
- Use separate secrets per environment

